{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>Ger, orphan, and widow.</b> They have no strength or help to publicize the matter to appeal against the judge. And one who lies with his father's wife, his sister, or his mother-in-law is not suspected of secluding with them. Also, one who lies with a beast — it does not cry out against the one who lies with it. And one who takes a bribe — it is a hidden matter. Except for idolatry and striking one's fellow, which is informant behavior, which is normally sometimes done openly and sometimes in secret — therefore 'in secret' is not said, for regarding transgressions done openly, he would not come to the principle that if he commits them openly, the court would punish him."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:54:26.548892867Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}